<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Kentigern</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 614</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Saint Mungo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint Kentigern, also called Mungo, was a 6th-century British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> in the kingdom of Strathclyde and is the patron saint of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glasgow">Glasgow</a>. His 12th-century Life by Jocelin of Furness tells of his miracles and his dealings with King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhydderch-hael">Rhydderch Hael</a>, though much of it is legend. His tomb lies in the crypt of Glasgow Cathedral.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-kentigern.jpg" alt="Saint Kentigern" width="320" height="375" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: dun_deagh · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Kentigern,_better_known_as_Mungo._Founder_and_patron_saint_of_Glasgow._(10062429595).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Rhydderch Hael, a king of the late 6th century, appears in the lives of Columba and <b>Kentigern</b>, the patron saint of Glasgow.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-strathclyde">Kingdom of Strathclyde</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Culross, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glasgow">Glasgow</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=56.06,-3.63&amp;year=604" aria-label="Culross on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4471 255 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Saint Kentigern"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4921 525h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4921 525h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=56.06,-3.63&amp;year=604">What was here in 604 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
